.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KUBE-LOAD-IMAGES 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kube-load-images
.Nd load the container images an offline cluster needs into containerd
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar directory
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
imports every
.Pa *.tar
in
.Ar directory ,
by default
.Pa /root/darksite/k8s-images ,
into containerd's
.Ql k8s.io
namespace with
.Ql ctr images import ,
so that a node with no internet can start or join a cluster.
It counts what imported against what it was given and names each archive
that did not.
.Pp
A directory that is missing or empty is not an error: it says so, and
the node pulls from the internet as it otherwise would.
It runs itself under
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print its description and exit 0, without root.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when every archive imported, or there were none; 1 when
.Xr ctr 8
is missing or any archive did not import.
.Sh EXAMPLES
In a Fedora 44 container, with three empty archives:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kube-load-images /nowhere
[kube-load-images] No pre-pulled images found at /nowhere — will pull from internet
# (exited 0)
# kube-load-images /img
[kube-load-images] ctr not found — containerd not installed?
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Pp
The same, with
.Xr ctr 8
replaced by a script that refuses
.Pa cilium.tar :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kube-load-images /img
ctr: unrecognized image format
[kube-load-images] Loaded 2 of 3 container image archives into containerd
[kube-load-images] FAILED to import: cilium.tar
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ctr 8 ,
.Xr kube-cluster 8 ,
.Xr kube-network 8
.Sh HISTORY
Until 2026-09-27 it counted the archives it tried, not the ones that
imported, and ignored failures: a golden reported every image loaded
while Cilium's, saved by digest with no name, gave containerd nothing it
could find.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Only
.Pa *.tar
files are imported; anything else in the directory is ignored and, if it
is all there is, reported as
.Dq Loaded 0 of 0 .
